嗯，那是食用油、湿巾和其他卫生用品的混合物。

503
00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:16.280
Oh, God.
哦，天哪。

504
00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:23.420
It was 250 meters long, which is about two and a half American football fields.
它长达250米，大约相当于两个半美式足球场。

505
00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:30.400
And it weighed 130 tons or about the same as 11 double-decker buses.
而且它重达130吨，或者说大约相当于11辆双层巴士的重量。

506
00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:32.060
Oh, my gosh.
哦，我的天呐。

507
00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:45.300
The term Fatberg was first used to describe the rock-like lumps of cooking fat that used to wash up on British beaches because people would pour their cooking fat down the drain.
“巨型油块”这个词最初是用来形容过去被冲上英国海滩的、像石头一样的食用油块，因为人们会把食用油倒入下水道。

508
00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:53.720
But now it's been adopted by sewer workers to describe sewer clogs caused by people pouring their grease down the drain.
但现在它被下水道工人用来形容人们将油脂倒入下水道而造成的下水道堵塞。

509
00:21:53.940 --> 00:21:59.500
And then it's sort of like coagulating with other things that aren't degrading quickly.
然后它就会和其它不易降解的东西凝结在一起。

510
00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:06.240
Actually, London has had a lot of them, but this Whitechapel Fatberg was the biggeSt.
事实上，伦敦已经出现过很多这种东西，但这个怀特chapel的巨型油块是最大的。

511
00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:10.880
