00:27:21.500 --> 00:27:22.060
It's great.
太棒了。

660
00:27:22.420 --> 00:27:23.720
I like their dynamic.
我喜欢她们之间的化学反应。

661
00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:24.960
They're both really funny.
她们两个都超级搞笑。

662
00:27:25.240 --> 00:27:25.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

663
00:27:26.360 --> 00:27:27.780
I loved the braid.
我很喜欢那个辫子。

664
00:27:27.780 --> 00:27:29.060
It's not her hair.
那不是她的头发。

665
00:27:29.500 --> 00:27:36.700
So I'm like, she just sometimes elects to wear those attachable ponytail braid things.
所以我心想，她有时只是选择戴那种可拆卸的马尾辫假发。

666
00:27:36.920 --> 00:27:42.040
It looks like the thing that, like, if you have a daughter and she's in her frozen stage
看起来就像那种，如果你有个女儿，她正处于《冰雪奇缘》的迷恋期

667
00:27:42.040 --> 00:27:47.160
and she wants to have the long Elsa braid that comes down and goes over her shoulder.
并且她想要一根长长的、垂下来搭在肩膀上的艾莎辫子。

668
00:27:47.160 --> 00:27:49.040
And then we clip it to the back of her hair.
然后我们把它夹在她脑后。

669
00:27:49.180 --> 00:27:49.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

670
00:27:49.900 --> 00:27:55.640
It reminded me of one of my early Yankee swap parties and you won the fake hair ponytail.
这让我想起我早期的一次洋基换物派对，你赢得了那个假发马尾。

671
00:27:55.980 --> 00:27:56.080
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

672
00:27:56.380 --> 00:27:57.740
I won one of those.
我赢过一个那样的。

673
00:27:57.740 --> 00:28:00.000
It was like as long as a horse's tail.
它长得就像马尾巴一样。

674
00:28:00.260 --> 00:28:01.000
It really was.
真的就是这样。

675
00:28:01.000 --> 00:28:02.120
I have a picture of you.
我有一张你的照片。

676
00:28:02.260 --> 00:28:04.180
You attached it that night at the party.
你那天晚上在派对上把它戴上了。

677
00:28:04.360 --> 00:28:05.500
You wore it for the rest of the night.
你整个晚上都戴着它。

678
00:28:05.500 --> 00:28:10.720
I have a picture of you sort of like over the shoulder with your giant horse ponytail.
我有一张照片，是你把那个巨大的马尾搭在肩上的样子。

679
00:28:11.380 --> 00:28:12.600
Whatever happened to that?
那个后来怎么处理了？

680
00:28:12.800 --> 00:28:13.360
I don't know.
我不知道。

681
00:28:13.440 --> 00:28:14.140
You took it home.
你把它带回家了。

682
00:28:14.300 --> 00:28:14.720
I did.
我确实带了。

683
00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:16.420
I didn't find it at my house.
我在自己家里没找到它。

684
00:28:16.520 --> 00:28:16.900
You know what?
你知道吗？

685
00:28:17.000 --> 00:28:18.160
That might have been disposable.
那个可能是用完就扔的。

686
00:28:18.880 --> 00:28:20.580
Oh, I think it was disposable.
哦，我觉得是一次性的。

687
00:28:20.880 --> 00:28:21.160
Might have been.
可能是吧。

688
00:28:21.460 --> 00:28:26.180
A lot of people that night, if they didn't like the gift they got, they hid it around my house.
那天晚上很多人，如果他们不喜欢得到的礼物，就会把它藏在我家各处。

689
00:28:26.820 --> 00:28:30.580
And I found it like months and months later, I would find things.
然后我会在好几个月后发现，我会找到一些东西。

690
00:28:30.780 --> 00:28:34.480
Well, you know, we've taken over the Yankee swap Christmas party tradition now.
嗯，你知道的，我们现在已经接管了洋基换物圣诞派对的传统。

691
00:28:34.480 --> 00:28:35.980
Yes, you do it with kids.
对，你们是跟小孩子一起玩。

692
00:28:36.180 --> 00:28:37.500
Mine was like rowdy adults.
我那时候都是成年人，闹得很凶。

693
00:28:37.800 --> 00:28:42.520
Yeah, but we get a lot of things left at our house, too, every year.
对，但我们家每年也会留下很多东西。

694
00:28:42.780 --> 00:28:44.660
Well, hopefully not on purpose.
好吧，希望不是故意的。

695
00:28:45.120 --> 00:28:51.220
Well, one year, Oscar's daughter won a sequined pillow.
嗯，有一年，奥斯卡的女儿赢了一个亮片枕头。

696
00:28:51.780 --> 00:28:56.760
It was like one of those pillows where like it's red, but then if you swipe up the sequins,
就是那种红色的枕头，如果你把亮片往上一抹，

697
00:28:56.900 --> 00:28:57.720
then it's something else.
就会变成别的图案。

698
00:28:57.720 --> 00:29:01.660
It was just a picture of Nicolas Cage that got left behind.
结果留下来的是一张尼古拉斯·凯奇的照片。

699
00:29:01.660 --> 00:29:03.500
And we get it out every Christmas now.
我们现在每年圣诞节都会把它拿出来。

700
00:29:03.500 --> 00:29:05.240
And they think it's really funny.
而且他们觉得这超级搞笑。

701
00:29:05.480 --> 00:29:08.060
That's actually a really great Yankee swap gift.
这其实真的是个很棒的白象交换礼物。

702
00:29:08.180 --> 00:29:08.720
I agree.
我同意。

703
00:29:09.100 --> 00:29:14.400
Nicolas Cage sequined pillow that changes like what it looks like depending on the direction.
尼古拉斯·凯奇的亮片抱枕，图案会随着方向改变而变化。

704
00:29:14.720 --> 00:29:14.980
Yeah.
对啊。

705
00:29:15.340 --> 00:29:15.940
That's brilliant.
太绝了。

706
00:29:16.620 --> 00:29:17.180
All right.
行吧。

707
00:29:17.740 --> 00:29:21.380
Ned calls Nicole, Detrick, Adam, and Adalola into his office.
内德把妮可、迪特里克、亚当和阿达洛拉叫进办公室。

708
00:29:21.580 --> 00:29:24.180
He needs the whole team on this story.
他需要整个团队来跟进这个报道。

709
00:29:24.560 --> 00:29:27.260
Travis tries to come in and join the party, but Ned says,
特拉维斯试图加入进来，但内德说：

710
00:29:27.260 --> 00:29:32.680
I'm sorry, I'm going to need you to recuse yourself because this story would implicate
抱歉，我得请你回避，因为这个报道会牵涉到

711
00:29:32.680 --> 00:29:34.320
softies and some wrongdoing.
软心派和一些不当行为。

712
00:29:34.500 --> 00:29:37.620
And you work for the softie side exclusively.
而且你专门为软心派那边工作。

713
00:29:38.320 --> 00:29:40.560
So Travis is like, all right.
于是特拉维斯只好答应。

714
00:29:40.680 --> 00:29:43.520
He reluctantly gives up his self-made press badge.
他极不情愿地交出了自己做的记者证。

715
00:29:44.340 --> 00:29:46.260
Ken is going to come barreling in.
肯气势汹汹地冲了进来。

716
00:29:46.340 --> 00:29:48.580
And he's like, listen, you cannot do this.
他说，听着，你们不能这么做。

717
00:29:48.720 --> 00:29:50.660
I forbid you to do this story.
我禁止你们做这个报道。

718
00:29:50.920 --> 00:29:52.580
And Ned is pushing back.
内德则据理力争。

719
00:29:52.580 --> 00:29:55.460
And then finally, Ken's like, okay, he's going to play hardball.
最后，肯决定动真格的了。

720
00:29:55.620 --> 00:29:58.080
He's like, accountants, you work for both companies.
他说，会计们，你们为两家公司工作。

721
00:29:58.100 --> 00:29:59.520
You're going back to Switzerland.
你们回瑞士去吧。

722
00:29:59.520 --> 00:30:00.340
You're out of here.
你们被解雇了。

723
00:30:00.540 --> 00:30:03.280
And then he's like, Detrick, you are in sales.
然后他又说，迪特里克，你是做销售的。

724
00:30:03.440 --> 00:30:04.360
He pulls him out.
他把他拉了出来。

725
00:30:04.560 --> 00:30:07.020
You're going to go sell these hand mitts now.
你现在去卖这些手套。

726
00:30:07.420 --> 00:30:11.180
And then he makes the accountants leave because they work for both companies.
接着他赶走了会计们，因为他们为两家公司服务。

727
00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:15.940
So basically, it's just down to Mare, Ned, and Nicole.
所以基本上只剩下梅尔、内德和妮可了。

728
00:30:16.300 --> 00:30:17.620
Ken leaves Barry in charge.
肯留下巴里负责。

729
00:30:17.820 --> 00:30:22.340
And then Barry immediately kind of tells them to go write a story on Charlie's Angels.
然后巴里转头就让他们去写一篇关于《霹雳娇娃》的报道。

730
00:30:22.580 --> 00:30:25.420
So they're like, okay, basically, we're on our own here.
所以他们觉得，好吧，基本上我们得靠自己了。

731
00:30:26.740 --> 00:30:34.120
So now Ken is realizing that there is a paper trail that implicates him.
现在肯意识到有会牵连到他的纸质记录痕迹。

732
00:30:34.740 --> 00:30:37.600
He has co-signed every email.
他在每一封邮件上都联署了。

733
00:30:38.000 --> 00:30:39.500
He is so ridiculous.
他太荒谬了。

734
00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:41.240
It's so funny to me.
我觉得这太搞笑了。

735
00:30:41.500 --> 00:30:45.620
This whole talking head is brilliant because he basically says, you guys,
这段访谈简直绝了，因为他基本上说，你们这些家伙，

736
00:30:45.680 --> 00:30:50.140
he responds to every single email so that it can seem like it was partly his idea.
他回复了每一封邮件，好让人觉得这主意里也有他的一份功劳。

737
00:30:50.570 --> 00:30:50.820
Yeah.
对。

738
00:30:51.060 --> 00:30:53.800
So that when things succeed, he can be like, I was there all along.
这样当事情成功时，他就可以说，我一直都在场啊。

739
00:30:54.300 --> 00:30:55.500
Don't you know these people?
你们不认识这样的人吗？

740
00:30:55.720 --> 00:30:55.980
Yes.
认识。

741
00:30:56.160 --> 00:30:56.980
In our work.
在我们工作中。

742
00:30:57.200 --> 00:30:59.660
And not in our podcast work.
不是在我们做播客的工作中。

743
00:30:59.780 --> 00:30:59.920
Yeah.
对。

744
00:31:00.120 --> 00:31:01.680
But in the world of Hollywood.
而是在好莱坞的世界里。

745
00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:02.260
Yes.
对。

746
00:31:02.440 --> 00:31:07.420
There's always some person when you're trying to get some project off the ground,
总有那么一个人，当你想把某个项目推进时，

747
00:31:07.980 --> 00:31:10.640
that's just part of the reply all chain.
他们只是“回复所有人”邮件链里的一员。

748
00:31:10.860 --> 00:31:10.980
Yeah.
对。

749
00:31:10.980 --> 00:31:15.940
They do no real developing, no real producing, no real anything.
他们不搞实质开发，不搞实质制作，什么实质工作都不做。

750
00:31:15.940 --> 00:31:18.080
But they're CC'd on it.
但他们全被抄送在里面。

751
00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:18.460
Yeah.
是啊。

752
00:31:18.680 --> 00:31:20.980
And they just do the reply all with like, looks good.
然后他们就直接群发回复，比如，看起来不错。

753
00:31:21.620 --> 00:31:22.980
Loving this direction.
很喜欢这个方向。

754
00:31:23.380 --> 00:31:23.560
Yeah.
对。

755
00:31:24.160 --> 00:31:25.460
Way to go, guys.
干得好，伙计们。

756
00:31:25.780 --> 00:31:26.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

757
00:31:26.440 --> 00:31:27.280
Great idea.
好主意。

758
00:31:27.800 --> 00:31:31.680
And then somehow then they're part of the project.
然后不知怎么的，他们就成了项目的一部分。

759
00:31:32.680 --> 00:31:33.540
That's Ken.
那是肯。

760
00:31:33.860 --> 00:31:34.460
That's Ken.
那是肯。

761
00:31:34.520 --> 00:31:35.900
Ken's the reply all man.
肯就是那个喜欢群发回复的人。

762
00:31:36.100 --> 00:31:38.360
Ken's the reply all man, but he goes one step further.
肯是个群发回复达人，但他还要更进一步。

763
00:31:38.520 --> 00:31:40.900
He then prints out his reply all.
他甚至把自己的群发回复打印出来。

764
00:31:40.900 --> 00:31:47.600
Yeah, because he wants a paper trail to prove that he was part of all of these different ideas.
对，因为他想要留下纸质证据，证明自己参与了所有这些不同的创意。

765
00:31:47.980 --> 00:31:48.360
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

766
00:31:48.720 --> 00:31:51.080
But he actually generated zero ideas.
但他实际上一个创意都没出。

767
00:31:51.500 --> 00:31:56.400
So Ken decides he has to get rid of this elaborate paper trail that he's created.
所以肯决定，他必须除掉自己制造的这堆繁琐的书面证据。

768
00:31:56.400 --> 00:31:58.440
So he's going to try to enlist Travis.
于是他打算把特拉维斯拉进来帮忙。

769
00:31:58.720 --> 00:32:00.680
And they have this really fun back and forth.
他们有一段非常有趣的你来我往的对话。

770
00:32:00.940 --> 00:32:05.740
I really liked how he was like, will you help me get rid of this?
我真的很喜欢他说，你能帮我把这些处理掉吗？

771
00:32:05.740 --> 00:32:09.460
And Travis is like, yes, we're going to agree on a location.
然后特拉维斯说，行，我们先商定一个地点。

772
00:32:09.460 --> 00:32:11.700
But then when we get there, we'll go to a second location.
但等我们到了那儿，我们再去第二个地点。

773
00:32:12.240 --> 00:32:16.740
And then Ken is like, can we just go to a third location right off the top?
接着肯就说，我们能不能一开始就直接去第三个地点？

774
00:32:16.900 --> 00:32:19.420
They're having this like, yeah, let's get to it.
他们当时那种状态就像是，好吧，我们直奔主题吧。

775
00:32:20.780 --> 00:32:24.040
And finally, they're like, fine, we'll meet in the parking lot in 10 minutes.
最后他们说，好吧，十分钟后在停车场见。

776
00:32:24.580 --> 00:32:27.320
So Ned is now going to do a bold move, in my opinion.
所以在我看来，内德现在要采取一个大胆的举动了。

777
00:32:27.540 --> 00:32:31.640
He's going to give Mare and Nicole access to his old Softies email.
他要给梅尔和妮可开放他以前的 Softies 邮箱权限。

778
00:32:31.640 --> 00:32:36.120
I think they're trying to dig into this Softies email to see if they can find who's responsible
我觉得他们是想深入挖掘这个 Softies 邮箱，看看能不能找到究竟是谁

779
00:32:36.120 --> 00:32:37.120
for the man mitts.
制造了男式连指手套。

780
00:32:37.320 --> 00:32:37.540
Okay.
好的。

781
00:32:37.860 --> 00:32:39.640
They're doing some mom detective work here.
她们在这里做妈妈侦探的工作呢。

782
00:32:40.060 --> 00:32:41.880
But he's like, yeah, here's my emails.
但他却说，行，这就是我的邮件。

783
00:32:41.880 --> 00:32:42.560
Go through them.
你们随便查。

784
00:32:42.660 --> 00:32:43.700
I don't have anything to hide.
我没什么好隐瞒的。

785
00:32:44.120 --> 00:32:50.620
But what Nicole and Mare find actually is this, I don't even know what you would call it,
但妮可和梅尔实际发现的是这个，我都不知道该怎么称呼它了，

786
00:32:50.660 --> 00:32:50.780
Jenna.
珍娜。

787
00:32:50.900 --> 00:32:57.220
It's like an inspirational video where Ned is teaching like the salesman how to sell.
这就像是一个励志视频，内德在里面教那些销售人员怎么做销售。

788
00:32:57.220 --> 00:33:01.980
Like he's saying things like, you've just got to go figure out what starts your engine.
比如他说，你们只要去找出是什么点燃了你们的发动机。

789
00:33:01.980 --> 00:33:03.500
So let me hear your engines.
所以让我听听你们的发动机声响。

790
00:33:03.660 --> 00:33:04.520
Come on, guys.
来吧，伙计们。

791
00:33:04.700 --> 00:33:05.280
Open up, fellas.
敞开心扉，小伙子们。

792
00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:05.940
Vroom, vroom.
轰，轰。

793
00:33:06.360 --> 00:33:08.300
And then all these salesmen are going, vroom, vroom.
然后所有的销售人员都在喊，轰，轰。

794
00:33:08.680 --> 00:33:18.260
Yeah, I guess they discover that back in his days as a salesman, Ned was so good that the
对，我想他们发现内德在当销售员的那个年代太优秀了，以至于

795
00:33:18.260 --> 00:33:23.400
company asked him to make motivational videos for the rest of the sales team.
公司邀请他为其他销售团队制作励志视频。

796
00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:23.800
Yeah.
是啊。

797
00:33:23.800 --> 00:33:28.020
And so he's there and he's got this whole different persona.
所以他在那里面呈现出了一种完全不同的个人形象。

798
00:33:28.020 --> 00:33:30.620
He's got like flicked back hair.
他留着那种往后梳的头发。

799
00:33:30.960 --> 00:33:32.420
He's just like, boo, boo.
他就像是，布，布。

800
00:33:32.860 --> 00:33:34.220
Glyn, Gary, Glyn Ross.
格林，加里，格林·罗斯。

801
00:33:34.420 --> 00:33:35.660
Like you got to sail, sail.
就像你得扬帆起航，扬帆起航。

802
00:33:36.280 --> 00:33:38.680
Mare has a string of hilarious comments.
梅尔有一连串搞笑的评论。

803
00:33:38.940 --> 00:33:39.380
She does.
确实有。

804
00:33:39.580 --> 00:33:43.260
She says, you look like you, but like 25% more oily.
她说，你看起来还是你，但油腻了25%。

805
00:33:43.640 --> 00:33:45.000
You look flammable.
你看起来易燃易爆。

806
00:33:45.260 --> 00:33:48.620
You look like if Draco Malfoy had a cocaine problem.
你看起来就像德拉科·马尔福沾上了毒品。

807
00:33:48.980 --> 00:33:49.500
Yes.
没错。

808
00:33:49.500 --> 00:33:53.880
And he really gets his feelings hurt, but he's trying to act like his feelings aren't
而且他真的被伤了自尊，但他又试图装作

809
00:33:53.880 --> 00:33:54.140
hurt.
没受伤。

810
00:33:54.260 --> 00:33:55.820
And she's like, OK, look, I'm sorry.
然后她说，好吧，听着，我很抱歉。

811
00:33:55.940 --> 00:33:56.540
I hurt your feelings.
我伤害了你的感情。

812
00:33:56.640 --> 00:33:57.680
And he's like, no, not at all.
而他说，不，完全没有。

813
00:33:57.800 --> 00:33:58.600
I like being ribbed.
我喜欢开玩笑。

814
00:33:58.760 --> 00:34:00.720
You look like Macaulay Culkin now.
你现在看起来像麦考利·卡尔金。

815
