00:43:28.780 --> 00:43:34.560
That's actually a tiny body of water right in the middle of the universal lot.
那其实是环球影城外景地正中间的一小片水域。

1008
00:43:34.800 --> 00:43:41.860
We had to stick with a very specific area to shoot because there are satellite dishes in
我们只能在一个非常特定的区域拍摄，因为有一个方向有卫星天线，

1009
00:43:41.860 --> 00:43:49.040
one direction, there are buildings in another direction, and in a third direction were where
另一个方向有建筑，第三个方向则是

1010
00:43:49.040 --> 00:43:53.040
the trams go by on the universal tour.
环球影城观光电车行驶的地方。

1011
00:43:53.240 --> 00:43:56.820
So we were threading the needle in this little pond to shoot the scene.
所以我们是在这个小池塘里小心翼翼地夹缝求生来拍摄这场戏的。

1012
00:43:57.000 --> 00:44:03.460
The only reason that they let us sink these folders of paper that we had to weigh down to
他们允许我们把这些纸质文件夹沉入水底——我们得加重它们的重量

1013
00:44:03.460 --> 00:44:09.940
get them to sink was because they're ultimately getting rid of the pond and building stages
才能让它们沉下去——唯一的理由是他们最终打算填平这个池塘，并在上面

1014
00:44:09.940 --> 00:44:10.660
over them.
建造摄影棚。

1015
00:44:10.780 --> 00:44:17.600
So they allowed us to submerge the paper because they're cleaning it all out very soon.
所以他们允许我们把纸淹没在水里，因为他们很快就会把这里彻底清理干净。

1016
00:44:17.980 --> 00:44:19.200
I have a question.
我有个问题。

1017
00:44:19.820 --> 00:44:28.340
If you had to get rid of something, files, evidence, a body, how would you get rid of it?
如果你必须处理掉某些东西，比如文件、证据、一具尸体，你会怎么处理？

1018
00:44:28.960 --> 00:44:29.500
Well.
嗯。

1019
00:44:29.740 --> 00:44:30.780
Have you ever thought about that?
你以前想过这个吗？

1020
00:44:30.780 --> 00:44:37.280
I had never thought about it until we were doing some construction and we had some flooding
我以前从没想过，直到我们在搞建设时，后院

1021
00:44:37.280 --> 00:44:38.040
in our backyard.
发生了一些水淹的情况。

1022
00:44:38.380 --> 00:44:41.720
And so you can build a dry well.
所以你可以建一个渗水井。

1023
00:44:42.060 --> 00:44:46.360
So when there's a lot of rain here and, you know, we don't get a ton of rain, but then
每当这里下了很多雨——你知道的，我们这里雨水不多，但

1024
00:44:46.360 --> 00:44:50.860
all of a sudden we get like weeks of rain and like the ground can't sustain it.
突然间就会下好几个星期的雨，地面根本承受不住。

1025
00:44:51.980 --> 00:44:53.600
So we built this dry well.
于是我们建了这个渗水井。

1026
00:44:54.800 --> 00:44:58.980
And for those of you guys that don't know, a dry well is like 10 feet deep.
对于不知道的人来说，渗水井大概有10英尺深。

1027
00:44:59.520 --> 00:45:05.720
And you put these boulders of all these different sizes kind of stacked in sort of like a non-symmetrical
你把各种不同大小的巨石以某种非对称的方式

1028
00:45:05.720 --> 00:45:06.160
way.
堆叠在里面。

1029
00:45:06.700 --> 00:45:08.300
And it makes a crevasse.
这样就会形成一个裂缝。

1030
00:45:08.300 --> 00:45:13.060
So when the water starts piling in and your backyard is getting flooded with water, it
所以当水开始积聚，你的后院被水淹没时，

1031
00:45:13.060 --> 00:45:19.440
goes into this dry well and naturally trickles down slowly into the ground and the ground
水就会流入这个渗水井，然后自然缓慢地渗入地下，土地

1032
00:45:19.440 --> 00:45:26.600
absorbs it, which is great for all of the plants and everything because a lot of people when
会吸收它，这对所有的植物等等都非常好，因为很多人

1033
00:45:26.600 --> 00:45:32.240
it rains, they have like drains that go to the street and then the street goes into the
下雨时，他们有通往街道的排水沟，然后街道的水会流入

1034
00:45:32.240 --> 00:45:36.500
runoff and the ground doesn't get to recoup all that moisture, right?
径流中，而地面却无法重新吸收这些水分，对吧？

1035
00:45:36.760 --> 00:45:38.680
So we had this dry well built.
所以我们建了这个渗水井。

1036
00:45:39.640 --> 00:45:41.780
But when they were building it, it's crazy.
但他们建造它的时候，太疯狂了。

1037
00:45:41.920 --> 00:45:44.520
It's just an enormous hole in the ground.
那只是地下一个巨大的洞。

1038
00:45:44.620 --> 00:45:50.420
And I thought like if someone needed to get rid of something, they could put it at the
当时我想，如果有人需要处理掉什么东西，他们可以把它放在

1039
00:45:50.420 --> 00:45:51.380
bottom of this dry well.
这个渗水井的最底部。

1040
00:45:51.500 --> 00:45:52.460
No one's going to find it.
没有人会找到它。

1041
00:45:52.780 --> 00:45:54.100
Made me think of Tony Soprano.
这让我想起了托尼·索普拉诺。

1042
00:45:54.580 --> 00:45:56.200
That's what I'm saying, right?
这就是我要说的，对吧？

1043
00:45:56.520 --> 00:45:56.820
Yeah.
是啊。

1044
00:45:56.820 --> 00:45:59.040
I mean, there's nothing in my dry well.
我的意思是，我的渗水井里可什么都没有。

1045
00:45:59.300 --> 00:46:00.680
I just want to go on record.
我只是想表明立场。

1046
00:46:01.340 --> 00:46:01.580
Well.
嗯。

1047
00:46:03.400 --> 00:46:06.300
But yeah, they dump all the files into this pond.
不过没错，他们把所有的文件都倒进了这个池塘里。

1048
00:46:06.540 --> 00:46:07.020
They do.
确实如此。

1049
00:46:07.340 --> 00:46:09.500
And Ken thinks, well, now I'm good.
肯以为，好吧，现在我没事了。

1050
00:46:10.200 --> 00:46:11.300
He's not good.
他可有事了。

1051
00:46:11.520 --> 00:46:12.300
He's not good.
他可真行。

1052
00:46:12.560 --> 00:46:13.500
Saboteur Travis.
搞破坏的特拉维斯。

1053
00:46:14.360 --> 00:46:15.760
We'll find out later.
我们待会儿再看。

1054
00:46:16.180 --> 00:46:19.340
Well, I think we should check back in with stage mom Esmeralda.
我觉得我们应该再去了解一下星妈埃斯梅拉达的情况。

1055
00:46:20.840 --> 00:46:25.400
Oscar is going to notice Esmeralda kind of being ridiculous and he tries to comfort her
奥斯卡注意到埃斯梅拉达有点不可理喻，于是他试图去安慰她

1056
00:46:25.400 --> 00:46:26.720
son, Mateo.
的儿子马特奥。

1057
00:46:26.820 --> 00:46:30.740
He's like, do you know what gray rocking is?
他说，你知道什么是“灰岩法”吗？

1058
00:46:31.300 --> 00:46:32.580
And the kid's like, no.
这孩子说，不知道。

1059
00:46:32.780 --> 00:46:35.600
And he's like, listen, my mom was pretty toxic.
然后他说，听着，我妈以前挺有毒的。

1060
00:46:36.020 --> 00:46:37.120
She was a narcissiSt.
她是个自恋狂。

1061
00:46:37.120 --> 00:46:38.200
She loved drama.
她喜欢小题大做。

1062
00:46:38.460 --> 00:46:43.560
So whenever she got into one of her moods, I'd make myself as uninteresting as possible,
所以每当她闹情绪的时候，我就会尽量让自己变得毫无存在感，

1063
00:46:43.800 --> 00:46:45.580
like a little gray rock.
就像一块灰色的石头。

1064
00:46:46.700 --> 00:46:49.400
And Oscar's like, maybe I shouldn't have gotten myself involved.
奥斯卡就觉得，也许自找麻烦是不对的。

1065
00:46:49.580 --> 00:46:51.780
But, you know, I just want to give this kid a fighting chance.
但是，你知道的，我只是想给这孩子一个力争上游的机会。

1066
00:46:51.940 --> 00:46:54.300
By the way, my mom was not any of those things.
顺便说一句，我妈才不是那种人。

1067
00:46:54.420 --> 00:46:56.280
He was just trying to help out Mateo.
他只是想帮马特奥一把。

1068
00:46:56.820 --> 00:47:01.340
And then Mateo has a talking head where he's like, that old man is a narcissiSt.
然后马特奥对着镜头采访时说，那个老头子才是自恋狂。

1069
00:47:01.340 --> 00:47:04.000
If he thinks I'm going to listen to him over my own mom.
如果他觉得我会听他的而不听我妈的话。

1070
00:47:05.080 --> 00:47:07.200
You know, gray rocking is a real thing.
你知道的，“灰岩法”是真有其事。

1071
00:47:08.260 --> 00:47:08.740
No.
不是。

1072
00:47:09.080 --> 00:47:09.320
Yes.
是的。

1073
00:47:09.440 --> 00:47:12.220
It's a real way to handle narcissistic personalities.
这是应对自恋型人格的一种真实方法。

1074
00:47:12.600 --> 00:47:13.980
You become uninteresting.
你变得毫无趣味。

1075
00:47:13.980 --> 00:47:14.580
Yeah.
对。

1076
00:47:14.800 --> 00:47:16.020
I looked this up.
我查过这个。

1077
00:47:16.120 --> 00:47:23.840
In a nutshell, the gray rock technique is a method in which you do not emotionally respond
简而言之，“灰岩法”是一种方法，即当受到控制欲强或自恋的人操纵时，

1078
00:47:23.840 --> 00:47:28.600
when being manipulated by someone who is controlling or narcissistic.
你不会做出情绪上的反应。

1079
00:47:28.760 --> 00:47:31.680
It's exactly what Oscar says in the episode.
这正是奥斯卡在剧中所说的。

1080
00:47:32.080 --> 00:47:35.520
Because ultimately, narcissists want your full attention.
因为归根结底，自恋狂想要你完全的注意力。

1081
00:47:35.520 --> 00:47:40.880
And if you become emotionally detached, they will become disinterested in you and move on.
如果你变得冷漠疏离，他们就会对你失去兴趣并走开。

1082
00:47:41.040 --> 00:47:46.860
But the minute you engage, that's when they start ramping up and the situation can get
但只要你一搭理，他们就会开始变本加厉，情况就会变得

1083
00:47:46.860 --> 00:47:48.960
emotionally abusive and very manipulative.
带有情感虐待性质且极具操纵性。

1084
00:47:49.340 --> 00:47:55.900
The article that I read noted, using the gray rock method does not mean ignoring them.
我读的那篇文章指出，使用“灰岩法”并不意味着忽视他们。

1085
00:47:55.900 --> 00:47:59.040
Because if you ignore them, that can trigger them too.
因为如果你忽视他们，那也会刺激到他们。

1086
00:47:59.420 --> 00:47:59.600
Right.
对的。

1087
00:48:00.140 --> 00:48:04.840
The goal is, when speaking to them, use a dull voice.
目标是，和他们说话时，语调要平淡。

1088
00:48:05.120 --> 00:48:07.140
Keep a neutral look on your face.
保持面无表情。

1089
00:48:07.620 --> 00:48:11.200
Avoid eye contact and respond with just a few words.
避免眼神接触，回答只用几个字。

1090
00:48:11.980 --> 00:48:14.800
Also, do not ask them any questions.
还有，不要问他们任何问题。

1091
00:48:14.960 --> 00:48:17.020
Do not encourage them to elaborate.
不要鼓励他们详述。

1092
00:48:17.380 --> 00:48:19.820
Do not offer any details about your life.
不要透露你生活的任何细节。

1093
00:48:19.820 --> 00:48:25.980
Just be aloof and eventually they will grow bored and they will try to engage someone else.
只要冷漠以待，他们最终就会感到无聊，并转而去纠缠别人。

1094
00:48:26.460 --> 00:48:29.860
Also, do not reveal that you're doing this method.
另外，不要暴露你正在使用这种方法。

1095
00:48:30.160 --> 00:48:30.840
Oh, yeah.
噢，对。

1096
00:48:30.940 --> 00:48:31.120
No.
不是。

1097
00:48:31.760 --> 00:48:32.780
But it's a real thing.
但这是真的。

1098
00:48:32.900 --> 00:48:33.600
Gray rocking.
灰岩法。

1099
00:48:34.040 --> 00:48:39.560
I do find, as you were describing that, like when I encounter someone like that, I do just
我确实发现，正如你刚才所描述的那样，当我遇到这样的人时，我确实就会

1100
00:48:39.560 --> 00:48:40.260
shut down.
直接封闭自己。

1101
00:48:40.700 --> 00:48:41.880
Like I shut off.
就像我闭门谢客一样。

1102
00:48:42.120 --> 00:48:42.280
Yeah.
对。

1103
00:48:43.260 --> 00:48:46.720
So maybe I've been gray rocking in those moments and I didn't even realize it.
所以也许我在那些时刻一直在进行灰岩法应对，而我甚至都没意识到。

1104
00:48:46.720 --> 00:48:53.360
But it's hard because I've been in situations with people like that and they'll know your
但这就很难，因为我和那种人相处过，他们会知道你的

1105
00:48:53.360 --> 00:48:56.140
buttons and they'll purposely try to push them.
软肋，并故意去触碰它们。

1106
00:48:56.300 --> 00:48:59.700
Because they want some reaction, any reaction, good or bad.
因为他们想要某种反应，任何反应，无论是好的还是坏的。

1107
00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:00.220
Yeah.
对。

1108
00:49:00.480 --> 00:49:00.640
Yeah.
对。

1109
00:49:00.800 --> 00:49:02.520
So it's a hard method to do.
所以这是一种很难实行的方法。

1110
00:49:02.700 --> 00:49:02.860
Yeah.
对。

1111
00:49:03.360 --> 00:49:09.220
Well, one of the things that's a runner through this is Ned pushing back on Ken about writing
嗯，贯穿其中的一条线索是内德反过来质问肯关于写

1112
00:49:09.220 --> 00:49:10.980
this article and the truth teller.
这篇文章和那个说真话的人的事。

1113
00:49:11.240 --> 00:49:14.560
And finally, he gets to his breaking point and he's like, if you don't let me tell this
最后，他达到了崩溃的边缘，他说，如果你不让我讲这个

1114
00:49:14.560 --> 00:49:16.880
story, I'll quit running the paper.
故事，我就辞职不干了。

1115
00:49:17.480 --> 00:49:18.620
And so he does.
于是他真的这么做了。

1116
00:49:18.700 --> 00:49:21.340
And he makes this big speech to the bullpen.
他在大办公室里发表了一场慷慨激昂的演讲。

1117
00:49:21.460 --> 00:49:22.800
And no one really is that interested.
但其实根本没人在意。

1118
00:49:23.280 --> 00:49:27.640
Like he just goes, he makes it a real moment where he's like, this is it.
就像他只是去讲，把它变成了一个真正的时刻，他说，就是这样。

1119
00:49:27.840 --> 00:49:28.960
I have to quit.
我必须辞职。

1120
00:49:29.660 --> 00:49:32.080
And then he hands the reins over to Mare.
然后他把权柄交给了梅尔。

1121
00:49:32.660 --> 00:49:36.240
And without even missing a beat, Adam's like, will you let us know where to forward your
亚当甚至连节奏都没停一下，就说，能告诉我们把你的

1122
00:49:36.240 --> 00:49:36.820
last paycheck?
最后一份薪水寄到哪里吗？

1123
00:49:37.200 --> 00:49:38.540
Like it's already blip.
就像这事已经翻篇了。

1124
00:49:38.660 --> 00:49:39.160
You're gone.
你已经走了。

1125
00:49:39.160 --> 00:49:40.900
So now Mare's in charge.
所以现在梅尔掌权了。

1126
00:49:41.060 --> 00:49:45.780
Lucky for Mare, a drone is going to fly in to where she is and drop.
对梅尔来说幸运的是，一架无人机将飞到她所在的地方并掉落。

1127
00:49:45.780 --> 00:49:46.340
Very subtle.
非常微妙。

1128
00:49:46.700 --> 00:49:52.100
Who's going to notice this giant drone making a loud noise, hovering through the bullpen?
谁会注意到这个发出巨响、盘旋穿过大办公室的巨大无人机呢？

1129
00:49:52.220 --> 00:49:52.640
It's true.
确实。

1130
00:49:52.820 --> 00:49:58.760
Marrowly getting through the doorway, hanging from it, a long string with a paper clip holding
勉强穿过门口，上面挂着一根长绳，挂着一个回形针夹着

1131
00:49:58.760 --> 00:49:59.480
some files.
一些文件。

1132
00:49:59.720 --> 00:50:01.340
No one's going to notice this.
没有人会注意到这个。

1133
00:50:01.540 --> 00:50:02.860
Well, they're from Travis.
嗯，它们是特拉维斯送来的。

1134
00:50:03.140 --> 00:50:05.720
They're the files that he sneaked out of the boat.
这些是他从船上偷偷带出来的文件。

1135
00:50:06.560 --> 00:50:11.480
So now she has her evidence, her hard evidence, and she's going to go find Ken.
所以现在她有了证据，确凿的证据，她要去找肯。

1136
00:50:11.640 --> 00:50:12.700
He's in the commissary.
他在餐厅里。

1137
00:50:12.840 --> 00:50:15.440
He's at the counter getting ready to order some food.
他在柜台准备点些吃的。

1138
00:50:15.560 --> 00:50:22.780
And Mare taps him on the shoulder and he lets out this sound.
梅尔拍了拍他的肩膀，他发出了这样一个声音。

1139
00:50:23.500 --> 00:50:24.960
I think we need to hear it.
我觉得我们需要听听这个。

1140
00:50:26.020 --> 00:50:27.880
Try our new Greek bowl.
品尝我们的新款希腊碗。

1141
00:50:29.120 --> 00:50:31.080
There's always a bowl, isn't there, in America?
美国总是有各种碗，对吧？

1142
00:50:31.380 --> 00:50:32.880
Everything's bowls with you guys.
你们这些人什么都能做成碗装的。

1143
00:50:33.640 --> 00:50:34.560
Oh, hello.
哦，你好。

1144
00:50:38.280 --> 00:50:42.180
This reaction from him cracked me up.
他这个反应把我逗乐了。

1145
00:50:42.340 --> 00:50:43.700
I watched it a few times.
我看了好几遍。

1146
00:50:43.700 --> 00:50:45.060
It's so crazy.
太疯狂了。

1147
00:50:45.400 --> 00:50:47.300
I loved everything about this scene.
我很喜欢这个场景的一切。

1148
00:50:47.480 --> 00:50:50.620
We got this question from Yasmeen in Dallas who said,
我们收到了来自达拉斯的亚斯明的提问，她说，

1149
00:50:50.760 --> 00:50:54.060
I love how Ken screams when Mare taps him on the back.
我太喜欢梅尔拍肯后背时肯的尖叫声了。

1150
00:50:54.200 --> 00:50:55.080
I laughed out loud.
我忍不住笑出了声。

1151
00:50:55.300 --> 00:50:58.260
Did it say Ken screams in the script?
剧本里写着肯会尖叫吗？

1152
00:50:58.500 --> 00:51:00.340
And that was his interpretation?
那是他的理解发挥吗？

1153
00:51:00.580 --> 00:51:01.160
Hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1154
00:51:01.960 --> 00:51:03.880
I texted Chelsea about it.
我为此给切尔西发了短信。

1155
00:51:03.880 --> 00:51:09.100
She said it took quite a few takes before she was able to hold it together and make this happen.
她说她拍了好几次才忍住没笑场，把这幕拍了出来。

1156
00:51:09.240 --> 00:51:12.140
And I guess it was scripted.
我猜这确实是剧本里写好的。

1157
00:51:12.220 --> 00:51:12.900
It was scripted.
是剧本里写的。

1158
00:51:12.980 --> 00:51:17.440
I reached out to Matt Stone about it and he said there's actually two jump scares in this script.
我为此联系了马特·斯通，他说这个剧本里其实有两个惊吓镜头。

1159
00:51:17.800 --> 00:51:20.200
One at the very beginning and then this one.
一个在最开始，然后就是这个。

1160
00:51:20.440 --> 00:51:21.360
Here's what he had to say.
以下是他的说法。

1161
00:51:22.040 --> 00:51:26.720
There are actually two scares in the episode.
这一集里其实有两个惊吓点。

1162
00:51:26.980 --> 00:51:35.800
At the beginning, Ned is startled by Mare when he's in the archive room and he discovers that she's been sleeping there and he gives a scream.
在开头，内德在档案室里被梅尔吓了一跳，他发现梅尔一直睡在那里，然后他尖叫了一声。

1163
00:51:36.040 --> 00:51:45.840
And then later on, when Mare sneaks up and startles Ken, when she ultimately asks him to give Ned his job back.
然后在后来，当梅尔悄悄走过去吓了肯一跳时，她最终要求肯把内德的工作还给他。

1164
00:51:45.840 --> 00:51:49.060
Both of those scenes were written by Michael Komen.
这两场戏都是迈克尔·科门写的。

1165
00:51:49.420 --> 00:51:56.700
He was very excited to get a very specific reaction from the actors and that all came from him.
他非常渴望从演员那里得到一种非常具体的反应，这完全是他的主意。

1166
00:51:57.240 --> 00:52:02.140
Okay, so are we learning that Michael Komen likes a jump scare?
好吧，所以我们的意思是迈克尔·科门喜欢突如其来的惊吓？

1167
00:52:02.340 --> 00:52:04.920
Is he like a horror movie buff?
他是个恐怖片迷吗？

1168
00:52:05.280 --> 00:52:06.520
I wonder.
我很好奇。

1169
00:52:07.020 --> 00:52:08.260
You love a jump scare.
你很喜欢这种突然的惊吓。

1170
00:52:08.680 --> 00:52:11.780
I don't mind a jump scare, like in a scary movie.
我不介意这种惊吓，比如在恐怖电影里。

1171
00:52:12.520 --> 00:52:14.280
Sure, I hate them.
当然，我很讨厌这种桥段。

1172
00:52:15.240 --> 00:52:16.480
Like, you know what I hate?
比如，你知道我最讨厌什么吗？

1173
00:52:16.940 --> 00:52:27.140
I hate when someone at night goes down in the kitchen for a snack and they open the fridge and then they shut the fridge and the person's right there.
我讨厌大晚上有人去厨房找零食，他们打开冰箱，然后关上冰箱，那个人就站在那里。

1174
00:52:27.660 --> 00:52:28.840
I hate it.
我讨厌这样。

1175
00:52:28.960 --> 00:52:29.640
You hate that.
你讨厌那样。

1176
00:52:30.780 --> 00:52:32.500
I'm just waiting the whole time.
我全程都在干等着。

1177
00:52:32.660 --> 00:52:33.360
They're going in the kitchen.
他们正往厨房走去。

1178
00:52:33.520 --> 00:52:34.780
I'm like, don't go, don't go, don't go.
我就想，别去，别去，别去。

1179
00:52:34.960 --> 00:52:35.860
Don't open the fridge.
别开冰箱。

1180
00:52:36.100 --> 00:52:37.060
Someone's in the bathroom.
有人在浴室里。

1181
00:52:37.260 --> 00:52:37.960
They shut the mirror.
他们关上镜子柜。

1182
00:52:39.160 --> 00:52:41.160
And someone's in the mirror behind them.
结果镜子里他们身后站着个人。

1183
00:52:41.440 --> 00:52:41.740
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1184
00:52:43.140 --> 00:52:46.860
Well, listen, Mare is going to sit Ken down.
好吧，听着，梅尔要把肯叫坐下来。

1185
00:52:47.020 --> 00:52:47.340
Yeah.
对。

1186
00:52:47.460 --> 00:52:49.220
And she's going to say, I have evidence.
然后她会说，我有证据。

1187
00:52:49.320 --> 00:52:53.800
I know that your fingerprints are all over the prototype for man mitts.
我知道男士连指手套原型上到处都是你的指纹。

1188
00:52:53.900 --> 00:52:55.820
You signed off on all of this.
这一切你都签字同意了。

1189
00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:56.520
Busted.
抓个正着。

1190
00:52:56.980 --> 00:53:00.060
And she's like, here's what I'm going to do.
然后她说，我打算这么做。

1191
00:53:00.060 --> 00:53:08.900
I'm going to forget all this if you let us publish this article and you let Ned come back so that he doesn't look like a wuss.
如果你让我们发表这篇文章，并且让内德回来，这样他就不会显得像个懦夫，我就把这一切既往不咎。

1192
00:53:08.900 --> 00:53:10.960
And Ken's like, here's the deal.
然后肯就说，情况是这样的。

1193
00:53:11.320 --> 00:53:12.840
We're all in this together.
我们都在同一条船上。

1194
00:53:12.840 --> 00:53:14.900
We're on the same sinking ship.
我们都在这艘正在下沉的破船上。

1195
00:53:15.120 --> 00:53:19.580
Because if Softies goes down, then the paper is gone.
因为如果软乎乎公司倒闭了，那报纸也就没了。

1196
00:53:20.300 --> 00:53:27.380
So we have all this back inventory now, these man mitts we can't get rid of, and it's going to hemorrhage the company.
所以我们现在积压了所有这些库存，这些卖不出去的男士连指手套，这会给公司造成严重的亏损。

1197
00:53:28.180 --> 00:53:30.260
So they decide, you know what?
所以他们决定，你知道吗？

1198
00:53:30.880 --> 00:53:32.180
They're going to reach out to Ned.
他们要去找内德。

1199
00:53:32.360 --> 00:53:35.000
He is the salesman of all salesmen, right?
他可是销售中的销售天才，对吧？

1200
00:53:35.380 --> 00:53:35.620
Yeah.
对。

1201
00:53:35.840 --> 00:53:36.520
Vroom, vroom.
轰，轰。

1202
00:53:37.000 --> 00:53:39.440
They're going to ask him to help save the company.
他们要请他帮忙拯救公司。

1203
00:53:39.720 --> 00:53:41.540
He takes such pride in it, lady.
他对此感到非常骄傲，女士。

1204
00:53:41.880 --> 00:53:42.920
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

1205
00:53:42.940 --> 00:53:44.560
I love this series of scenes.
我很喜欢这一组镜头。

1206
00:53:44.740 --> 00:53:46.040
So here's what they come up with.
所以他们想出了这个主意。

1207
00:53:46.040 --> 00:53:51.700
They're going to repackage the mitts as like a dish towel.
他们要把手套重新包装成洗碗巾之类的东西。

1208
00:53:51.920 --> 00:53:52.700
Like kitchen wipes.
就像厨房湿巾一样。

1209
00:53:52.800 --> 00:53:53.700
Yes, kitchen wipes.
对，厨房湿巾。

1210
00:53:53.840 --> 00:53:54.880
That you throw in the trash.
用完就直接扔进垃圾桶。

1211
00:53:55.100 --> 00:53:59.400
Ned says they're all-purpose, all-surface, sturdy, ergonomic kitchen wipes.
内德说这是多功能、全表面、坚固且符合人体工程学的厨房湿巾。

1212
00:53:59.580 --> 00:54:01.440
And he is on fire.
而且他状态火热。

1213
00:54:01.440 --> 00:54:02.600
He is selling them.
他在拼命推销。

1214
00:54:02.680 --> 00:54:05.640
They get up to $200,000 in sales.
他们的销售额达到了20万美元。

1215
00:54:05.640 --> 00:54:06.100
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1216
00:54:06.100 --> 00:54:08.040
They're ringing that gong like crazy.
他们像疯了似地敲着那个锣。

1217
00:54:08.320 --> 00:54:09.940
Here's my hot take.
这是我的犀利观点。

1218
00:54:10.140 --> 00:54:10.460
What?
什么？

1219
00:54:11.460 --> 00:54:13.580
Should Ned be in sales?
内德应该去做销售吗？

1220
00:54:13.580 --> 00:54:13.940
Yes.
是的。

1221
00:54:14.000 --> 00:54:14.820
Why isn't he?
他为什么不去做呢？

1222
00:54:14.820 --> 00:54:16.760
Lean into what you're good at, Ned.
发挥你擅长的领域吧，内德。

1223
00:54:16.960 --> 00:54:18.380
He also seems happier.
而且他看起来更开心了。

1224
00:54:18.660 --> 00:54:18.940
Yes.
是的。

1225
00:54:19.020 --> 00:54:21.000
His whole disposition changes.
他整个人都变了。

1226
00:54:21.400 --> 00:54:21.620
Yeah.
对。

1227
00:54:21.780 --> 00:54:24.000
He's like peppy and spirited.
他变得精气神十足，充满活力。

1228
00:54:24.240 --> 00:54:27.460
He's smiling for the first time in eight episodes.
他八集以来第一次笑了。

1229
00:54:28.060 --> 00:54:32.000
I think Mare should run the paper and Ned should run sales.
我觉得梅尔应该管理报社，内德应该负责销售。

1230
00:54:32.320 --> 00:54:32.880
Yes.
没错。

1231
00:54:34.260 --> 00:54:34.820
100%.
百分之百。

1232
00:54:34.820 --> 00:54:35.360
Yeah.
对。

1233
00:54:35.640 --> 00:54:38.760
And then they can date and it won't be weird because they're in different departments.
然后他们就可以约会了，而且因为不在同一个部门，也不会觉得尴尬。

1234
00:54:39.680 --> 00:54:41.460
Well, we just solved all the probleMs.
好吧，我们刚刚把所有问题都解决了。

1235
00:54:41.780 --> 00:54:41.880
We did.
确实解决了。

1236
00:54:42.660 --> 00:54:43.540
Look at us.
看看我们。

1237
00:54:43.540 --> 00:54:45.600
If you need us, we're right here, guys.
如果需要我们，我们就一直在，伙计们。

1238
00:54:45.840 --> 00:54:47.340
What you got going on?
你们在忙什么呢？

1239
00:54:48.760 --> 00:54:51.240
Ned's going to finish the episode with the talking head.
内德要在这一集的单人访谈中收尾。

1240
00:54:51.380 --> 00:54:56.040
He says, you know, there are several ways to save a paper from writing an important article
他说，你知道的，拯救一家报社有很多种方法，从写一篇重要的文章

1241
00:54:56.040 --> 00:55:00.060
to quitting to selling a buttload of rebranded kitchen wipes.
到辞职，再到卖出海量的重新贴牌的厨房湿巾。

1242
00:55:00.340 --> 00:55:01.720
Today, it was all three.
今天，这三样他都做了。

1243
00:55:02.680 --> 00:55:04.440
Well, there you have it, folks.
好了，事情就是这样，各位。

1244
00:55:05.080 --> 00:55:08.840
I, for one, now want to see the fatberg.
我个人现在非常想见识一下那座脂肪山。

1245
00:55:09.300 --> 00:55:10.680
Sam, I think you're with me.
萨姆，我觉得你跟我是一伙的。

1246
00:55:10.880 --> 00:55:12.020
We don't have a lot of time.
我们时间不多了。

1247
00:55:12.280 --> 00:55:12.660
Right.
对。

1248
00:55:12.720 --> 00:55:13.340
It's shrinking.
它在缩小。

1249
